     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily or about 567 mg three times daily. Standard tablet sizes would make 850 mg twice daily the practical choice.\n- **Another dose.** Metformin is usually started at 500 mg once or twice daily and increased gradually.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
