     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1,700 mg three times daily (5,100 mg/day) is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. I can't think of a clinical situation where that would be therapeutic, and the main risk is serious: lactic acidosis. This patient has normal kidney and liver function, so nothing in the chart offsets that risk.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can do this now, for example 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower starting dose if the patient is new to metformin.\n- **Call pharmacy or the attending.** If you think there's a specific reason for the higher dose, they can review it and enter it through their own channel.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
